  "methodology": [
    "Independently measured this pink reference at 5x and 10x zoom with labeled 5/10-pixel source-coordinate grids; none of the prior white character coordinates were reused.",
    "Generated closed lashes measured separately with 20-pixel grid; checked per-column dark warm pixel extents to distinguish eyelash ink from pink eyelid/brow and hair lines.",
    "Generated mouth checked per-row warm/pink color extents. Original smile checked per-row feature pixels.",
    "Polygons are manual feature segmentation proposals, with approximately 1..2 reference-pixel and 2..4 generated-pixel boundary uncertainty because anti-aliasing and overlaid fringe obscure exact contours.",
    "Eye opening corner anchors and full eyelash ink terminals are intentionally distinct. A blink should keep opening contacts at the same character locations while lash wings taper outside those contacts.",
    "Polygons alone do not certify animation continuity. Composite neutral source, half-blink 0.75/0.5/0.25/0, winks, head XY extremes, and MouthOpen x MouthSmile grid on light/dark/checkerboard backgrounds before finalizing."
  ]
